WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:06.240
So I talked about that having a job we
love is a right, not a privilege

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:08.298
but there are many people who push back
and say to me,

00:00:08.298 --> 00:00:09.540
"Yeah but having a job you love really is a luxury

00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:15.809
and a lot of people just need a job to survive."

00:00:15.809 --> 00:00:18.240
At some level everybody needs a job to survive

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:22.300
and regardless of what our needs are 
and where we work,

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:24.720
wouldn't we rather work for companies that care about us as human beings?

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:30.210
A company doesn't have to be glamorous for us to 
love the work.

00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:32.482
There are many companies that do
glamorous things

00:00:32.482 --> 00:00:33.962
that are terrible places to work

00:00:33.962 --> 00:00:36.700
and there are lots of companies 
that do some pretty mundane things

00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:42.180
that just make some random widget, 
that are wonderful places to work.

00:00:42.180 --> 00:00:44.700
This is what my whole movement is about.

00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:49.300
I want to create change, 
I want to drive change in the business world,

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:51.540
so that everyone,
regardless of what our income is,

00:00:51.540 --> 00:00:53.081
regardless of what we're making,

00:00:53.081 --> 00:00:55.300
regardless what our position inside the organization is,

00:00:55.300 --> 00:01:01.100
that every single one of us gets to work at a place

00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:04.710
where we feel that people
view us and treat us like human beings

00:01:04.710 --> 00:01:09.880
rather than some disposable thing on a
financial statement.

00:01:09.880 --> 00:01:13.440
So to all those people who say,

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:15.600
"Yeah but some people just need a job to survive."

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:17.000
I say, absolutely.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:19.376
And they should have the opportunity to work in a place

00:01:19.376 --> 00:01:21.400
that they love going to work also.

